"lower in AD","module_padj":0.137528,"module_significant":false}],"degas_bulk_de":false,"drug_target":false}},"description":[{"gene_id":"ENSG00000149451","entrez_id":["80332"],"uniprot":["Q9BZ11"],"ncbi_summary":"This gene encodes a member of the ADAM (a disintegrin and metalloprotease domain) family. Members of this family are membrane-anchored proteins structurally related to snake venom disintegrins, and have been implicated in a variety of biological processes involving cell-cell and cell-matrix interactions, including fertilization, muscle development, and neurogenesis. This protein is a type I transmembrane protein implicated in asthma and bronchial hyperresponsiveness. Alternative splicing results in multiple transcript variants encoding different isoforms. [provided by RefSeq, Sep 2013].","ncbi_source":"NCBI Gene summary (RefSeq), via MyGene.info","uniprot_function":[{"accession":"Q9BZ11","text":"Metalloprotease that cleaves and sheds the ectodomains of cell-surface proteins and thereby contributes to angiogenesis, cell differentiation, inflammation, and cell proliferation (PubMed:14676211, PubMed:33982767). Modulates the activity of adhesion molecules and cytokines by generating soluble forms, leading to either attenuation of cell-surface signaling or initiation of downstream intracellular signaling pathways. For instance, acts as a constitutive sheddase of kit ligand/KITLG (PubMed:14676211). Promotes and maintains a proliferative phenotype in vascular smooth muscle cells through regulation of the PI3K/AKT and ERK signaling pathways (PubMed:33982767). Additionally, enhances cell migration and regulates cytokine secretion during airway vascular remodeling via the same signaling cascades (PubMed:36091328)."}],"uniprot_source":"UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot Function, release 2026_04","retrieved":"2026-10-21"}],"structures":[],"alphafold_accessions":[]}